{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuo1uc1QziJS2vmpuXPT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Generally, no. `@vitest/runner` is an internal package that `vitest` already depends on, and Vitest re-exports the public pieces. Test APIs (`test`, `describe`, hooks, `TestContext`, etc.) come from `vitest`. Lower-level runner utilities for custom runners or tasks (e.g. `getCurrentSuite`, `createTaskCollector`, `setFn`) come from `vitest/suite`, and runner types are available from `vitest`.\n\nAdding `@vitest/runner` as a separate dependency risks installing a version that doesn't match your `vitest` version, which can cause subtle breakage like duplicate module instances or mismatched internal state. Only add it directly if you need something that genuinely isn't re-exported. In that case, pin it to exactly the same version as `vitest`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2244,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2244},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"09857f59-2e85-492d-9047-5357b4ba665b","uuid":"d9280dd7-6595-482d-9b35-734bcfdb2e0a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:09:53.217Z","request_id":"req_011Cfuo1uPcZw2bohuKYuUqh"}
